---
import FlowFeaturePage from '../../components/flow/FlowFeaturePage.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../../components/flow/FlowDetail.astro';
import { FLOW_V16_SHOTS as shots } from '../../data/flow-v16';
import jobsMap from '../../assets/flow/shots/v17-jobs-map.webp';
import reviewChart from '../../assets/flow/shots/v17-review-selected-chart.webp';
const folders = [
  ['Stock Portfolio', 'Bring holdings, allocation, market context and headlines into one dashboard.'],
  ['Tax Advisor', 'Organize tax inputs and estimates, with the IRS pages you choose to watch.'],
  ['Household Budget', 'Compare spending with the plan, track income and read the savings rate.'],
  ['Job Search', 'See applications and next steps on a timeline, with careers pages and resume files alongside.'],
  ['Competitor Watch', 'Track your comparison table and notice changes on named public pricing pages.'],
  ['Team Status', 'Bring each person’s update file into one table, with confidence and milestones.'],
  ['Living Document Starter', 'Copy a folder with each construct wired once. Keep what your routine needs.'],
];
---
<FlowFeaturePage slug="living-documents" title="Flow Living Documents · Work that keeps up · Orionfold" description="Start with 24 Living Documents in Flow 1.7 for Mac. Inspect Jobs, connect data to charts and tables, and review changes in files you own.">
  <section class="flow-feature-section" id="connected-to-source"><div class="flow-feature-inner flow-feature-grid">
    <div class="flow-feature-copy"><p class="of-eyebrow">01 · Connect the source</p><h2 class="of-display">Change the data. The page follows.</h2><p>A chart or table can draw from a file in the document's folder. Change that source and Flow redraws the bound block. Your title, chart type and table layout stay yours.</p><p>Flow notices source changes as they happen, when you return to the app, on Refresh Folders and after the Night Shift. A source that changed while Flow was closed is picked up at launch.</p><p>The document remains <strong>ordinary Markdown</strong>. Its sources are files you can inspect and edit.</p></div>
    <FlowDetail src={reviewChart} alt="Flow 1.7 highlights the selected allocation chart beside its applied-change review in the Workbench." caption="Flow 1.7 (2173) · A selected chart and its review · Illustrative portfolio data" />
  </div></section>
  <section class="flow-feature-section" id="document-jobs"><div class="flow-feature-inner flow-feature-grid flow-feature-grid--reverse">
    <div class="flow-feature-copy"><p class="of-eyebrow">02 · Give it a job</p><h2 class="of-display">The routine belongs to the document.</h2><p>The document's Jobs open in the Workbench beside it. Use <strong>Edit</strong> to choose a step and its inputs, <strong>Relations</strong> to inspect declared reads and outputs, and <strong>Run</strong> to see the result.</p><ul><li><strong>Collect data</strong> reads a definition that says what to gather and where to save it.</li><li><strong>Watch sources</strong> compares named files, folders and HTTPS pages with the earlier copy.</li><li><strong>List a folder</strong> keeps filenames, sizes and dates in view.</li><li><strong>Overnight notes</strong> asks a configured local model to interpret the page's numeric evidence.</li></ul><p>Save changes to the Jobs, then choose <strong>Run Jobs</strong> for this document. Relations distinguishes a ready local input from a declared web source that has not been fetched. The Jobs map shows those dependencies; its arrows do not run another document.</p></div>
    <FlowDetail src={jobsMap} alt="Flow 1.7 shows the Portfolio Dashboard beside the Jobs Workbench, with declared inputs, a Collect data step and its outputs." caption="Flow 1.7 (2173) · Relations and the Jobs map · Illustrative portfolio example" />
  </div></section>
  <section class="flow-feature-section" id="seven-starting-points"><div class="flow-feature-inner"><p class="of-eyebrow">03 · Begin with a real routine</p><h2 class="of-display">24 starting points. Make one yours.</h2><p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">Choose <strong>Start with useful work</strong> to browse all 24 Living Documents. Search or explore four categories: Research &amp; Markets, Business &amp; Teams, Personal &amp; Money and Learn Flow. Five featured documents help you begin. Create an independent copy with its inputs and assets, then inspect its Jobs before running it.</p><p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">Here are seven examples from the library.</p><div class="mt-9 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">{folders.map(([name, description]) => <article class="flow-feature-card"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold">{name}</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-text-muted">{description}</p></article>)}</div><p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">These are editable examples with sample data. They organize your work; financial and tax examples do not replace qualified advice.</p></div></section>
  <section class="flow-feature-section" id="work-you-can-return-to"><div class="flow-feature-inner flow-feature-grid">
    <div class="flow-feature-copy"><p class="of-eyebrow">04 · Return with context</p><h2 class="of-display">A better place to pick up tomorrow.</h2><p>The document, the data and the next step stay together. The Night Shift reports what changed in the Morning Briefing, and marks applied changes for your review.</p><p>Select a change to inspect that part of the document. <strong>Keep</strong> records your review; <strong>Revert</strong> restores that part; <strong>Later</strong> leaves the decision pending. <strong>Document</strong> and <strong>Exact changes</strong> give you two ways to inspect it.</p><a class="of-text-action mt-6 inline-flex" href="/flow/night-shift/">See the Night Shift <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <FlowDetail src={shots.livingJobSearch} alt="A timeline shows application stages and dates in the Job Search example." caption="Earlier document detail · Flow 1.6 (1899) · Sample applications" />
  </div></section>
</FlowFeaturePage>
